.TH CUTKIND 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
CutKind \- What one cutscene step does
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqcutscene.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef enum { CUT_WAIT, CUT_MOVE, CUT_SAY, CUT_FADE_OUT, CUT_FADE_IN, CUT_CALL } CutKind;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
What one cutscene step does. Each kind reads different CutStep fields; the CUT_* macros fill them for you.
.SH VALUES
.TP
.B CUT_WAIT
pause for duration seconds
.TP
.B CUT_MOVE
ease *actor from where it is to `to` over duration seconds
.TP
.B CUT_SAY
show a dialog line (speaker, text) and wait for the player to dismiss it
.TP
.B CUT_FADE_OUT
fade the screen to black over duration seconds (the black stays until a fade in)
.TP
.B CUT_FADE_IN
fade from black back to the scene over duration seconds
.TP
.B CUT_CALL
call fn(e, ctx) once and move on immediately (change a level, give an item, play a sound)
.SH MODULE
cutscene (src/engine/cutscene/cutscene.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR CutStep (3),
.BR cutscene_start (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
